{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Sassy McGraw: Luminar Neo → Kohya LoRA → ComfyUI\n",
    "\n",
    "A practical Windows-first notebook for building a reusable archival colorization style from photographs colorized in Luminar Neo, then using that style with the Sassy McGraw identity LoRA.\n",
    "\n",
    "The governing idea is simple: Luminar provides the color reference, Kohya learns the colorization look, ComfyUI applies it to black-and-white inputs, and VHS damage is added afterward as a found-footage treatment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Fixed project paths\n",
    "\n",
    "Change only the paths in the next cell if your folders move. The Slayverse lore index is here:\n",
    "\n",
    "`C:\\runb2\\VUORSE-VORTEX\\Slayverse\\json\\slayverse_index_minified.json`\n",
    "\n",
    "The clean Sassy training set is here:\n",
    "\n",
    "`D:\\kohya_ss\\dataset\\sassy\\img\\10_sassy mcgraw woman`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "KOHYA = Path(r\"D:\\kohya_ss\")\n",
    "WORK = Path(r\"D:\\kohya_ss\\dataset\\slayverse_colorization\")\n",
    "BW_DIR = WORK / \"originals_bw\"\n",
    "COLOR_DIR = WORK / \"luminar_color\"\n",
    "CAPTION_DIR = WORK / \"captions\"\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR = Path(r\"D:\\ComfyUI312\\ComfyUI\\models\\loras\")\n",
    "LORE_INDEX = Path(r\"C:\\runb2\\VUORSE-VORTEX\\Slayverse\\json\\slayverse_index_minified.json\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for folder in (BW_DIR, COLOR_DIR, CAPTION_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR):\n",
    "    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Kohya:\", KOHYA)\n",
    "print(\"Luminar targets:\", COLOR_DIR)\n",
    "print(\"Lore index:\", LORE_INDEX)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Prepare the Luminar Neo pairs\n",
    "\n",
    "Put each original black-and-white image in `originals_bw` and its matching Luminar Neo colorized version in `luminar_color`. Use identical filenames:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "originals_bw\\frame_001.png\n",
    "luminar_color\\frame_001.png\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep the pairs aligned and exported at the same dimensions. The black-and-white files document the intended input; the Luminar files are the clean visual targets used for learning the colorization style. Do not bake VHS damage into these training targets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "bw = {p.stem for p in BW_DIR.glob(\"*\") if p.is_file()}\n",
    "color = {p.stem for p in COLOR_DIR.glob(\"*\") if p.is_file()}\n",
    "print(f\"black-and-white inputs: {len(bw)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Luminar targets: {len(color)}\")\n",
    "print(\"missing Luminar targets:\", sorted(bw - color))\n",
    "print(\"missing black-and-white inputs:\", sorted(color - bw))\n",
    "assert bw == color, \"Every pair must have the same filename stem.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Write captions for the Luminar targets\n",
    "\n",
    "Train the style adapter on the colorized images, not on the grayscale inputs. Use a dedicated trigger phrase so the color treatment can be turned on and off:\n",
    "\n",
    "`slayverse luminar color`\n",
    "\n",
    "Describe visible content and the color language. Keep the trigger phrase first. For Sassy images, retain the identity trigger separately: `sassy mcgraw, woman`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "captions = {\n",
    "    \"frame_001\": \"slayverse luminar color, sassy mcgraw, woman, 1970s television newsroom, warm muted broadcast colors, natural period skin tones, realistic archival colorization\",\n",
    "    \"frame_002\": \"slayverse luminar color, sassy mcgraw, woman, close documentary portrait, soft warm studio light, restrained historical color palette, realistic archival colorization\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for stem, caption in captions.items():\n",
    "    (CAPTION_DIR / f\"{stem}.txt\").write_text(caption, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Replace the example captions with one caption per Luminar target before training.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Caption rules\n",
    "\n",
    "- Use `slayverse luminar color` consistently.\n",
    "- Use `sassy mcgraw, woman` only on Sassy images.\n",
    "- Describe clothing, setting, lighting, and broad palette.\n",
    "- Avoid `vhs damage`, scan lines, rain, tracking errors, or tape noise. Those belong in post.\n",
    "- Avoid claiming exact historical colors when the source does not establish them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Create the Kohya configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the Luminar-colored images as the training images and their matching `.txt` files as captions. Start with a modest style LoRA: rank 16 or 32, 10–15 epochs, and checkpoint saves every 5 epochs. The output name below keeps the colorization adapter separate from the identity adapter.\n",
    "\n",
    "Save the following as `D:\\kohya_ss\\configs\\slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl.toml` and adjust only the dataset path if necessary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "config = r'''pretrained_model_name_or_path = \"D:/ComfyUI312/ComfyUI/models/checkpoints/RealVisXL_V5.0_fp16.safetensors\"\n",
    "train_data_dir = \"D:/kohya_ss/dataset/slayverse_colorization\"\n",
    "output_dir = \"D:/ComfyUI312/ComfyUI/models/loras\"\n",
    "logging_dir = \"D:/ComfyUI312/ComfyUI/models/loras/training_logs/slayverse_luminar_color\"\n",
    "output_name = \"slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl\"\n",
    "save_model_as = \"safetensors\"\n",
    "save_precision = \"bf16\"\n",
    "resolution = \"1024,1024\"\n",
    "enable_bucket = true\n",
    "min_bucket_reso = 512\n",
    "max_bucket_reso = 2048\n",
    "bucket_reso_steps = 64\n",
    "caption_extension = \".txt\"\n",
    "shuffle_caption = true\n",
    "keep_tokens = 3\n",
    "train_batch_size = 1\n",
    "epoch = 15\n",
    "save_every_n_epochs = 5\n",
    "seed = 4242\n",
    "learning_rate = 0.0001\n",
    "unet_lr = 0.0001\n",
    "text_encoder_lr = [0.00005, 0.00005]\n",
    "lr_scheduler = \"cosine\"\n",
    "optimizer_type = \"AdamW8bit\"\n",
    "mixed_precision = \"bf16\"\n",
    "cache_latents = true\n",
    "cache_latents_to_disk = true\n",
    "gradient_checkpointing = true\n",
    "max_data_loader_n_workers = 2\n",
    "persistent_data_loader_workers = true\n",
    "xformers = true\n",
    "no_half_vae = true\n",
    "network_module = \"networks.lora\"\n",
    "network_dim = 32\n",
    "network_alpha = 16\n",
    "training_comment = \"Slayverse archival colorization based on Luminar Neo references\"\n",
    "metadata_title = \"Slayverse Luminar Colorization SDXL LoRA\"\n",
    "metadata_author = \"Golden Wings Documentary\"\n",
    "metadata_description = \"Archival colorization look learned from creator-colorized Luminar Neo references\"\n'''\n",
    (KOHYA / \"configs\" / \"slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl.toml\").write_text(config, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "print(KOHYA / \"configs\" / \"slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl.toml\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Launch training\n",
    "\n",
    "From PowerShell, run the Kohya launcher from `D:\\kohya_ss`. Use the GUI if you want to inspect settings, or use the generated TOML through the LoRA tab. The intended output files are:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "D:\\ComfyUI312\\ComfyUI\\models\\loras\\slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl-000005.safetensors\n",
    "D:\\ComfyUI312\\ComfyUI\\models\\loras\\slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl-000010.safetensors\n",
    "D:\\ComfyUI312\\ComfyUI\\models\\loras\\slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl.safetensors\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare epoch 5, epoch 10, and the final checkpoint. The best one is the one that preserves the original face and structure while producing the Luminar-like color separation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Use it in ComfyUI\n",
    "\n",
    "Load a black-and-white photo into an SDXL img2img workflow. Use two LoRA loaders if Sassy is present:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Identity LoRA: `sassy_mcgraw_sdxl-000010.safetensors`, strength around `0.8–0.95`.\n",
    "- Colorization LoRA: `slayverse_luminar_color_sdxl.safetensors`, strength around `0.5–0.8`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Start with img2img denoise around `0.25–0.45`. Lower denoise preserves the original face and composition; higher denoise allows more color and lighting interpretation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reusable Sassy prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "sassy mcgraw, woman, slayverse luminar color, restored 1970s television news photograph, natural period skin tones, warm muted broadcast colors, brown suede vest, white mock turtleneck, gold chain necklace, golden angel wings brooch, realistic documentary photography, preserved facial structure, authentic archival colorization\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Reusable negative prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "oversaturated colors, neon colors, modern clothing, plastic skin, beauty filter, anime, illustration, altered facial structure, waxy face, color bleeding, chromatic artifacts, VHS tracking lines, tape damage, rain overlay\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Premade prompt cards\n",
    "\n",
    "### Anchor Desk\n",
    "`sassy mcgraw, woman, slayverse luminar color, seated at a 1970s newsroom desk, warm muted broadcast colors, brown suede vest, white mock turtleneck, golden angel wings brooch, serious expression, realistic archival documentary still`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Breaking News\n",
    "`sassy mcgraw, woman, slayverse luminar color, urgent live television news broadcast, standing beside a period newsroom monitor, restrained amber and teal color palette, dramatic studio lighting, realistic 1970s documentary photograph`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Field Report\n",
    "`sassy mcgraw, woman, slayverse luminar color, on-location television field report, period microphone, wind in her Farrah Fawcett hair, faded natural daylight, muted archival colors, realistic documentary photography`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Election Night\n",
    "`sassy mcgraw, woman, slayverse luminar color, 1970s election-night newsroom, wall of vintage monitors, papers and pencils on the desk, warm tungsten light, restrained period colorization, serious broadcast portrait`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Glamour Portrait\n",
    "`sassy mcgraw, woman, slayverse luminar color, polished 1970s television publicity portrait, Farrah Fawcett hair, warm skin tones, brown suede vest, gold jewelry, golden angel wings brooch, soft studio light, realistic archival color photograph`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Found-footage finishing\n",
    "\n",
    "Do not put `vhs damage` into the colorization training captions. After the color and identity pass is stable, add the found-footage treatment in the video/post stage: variable tape noise, tracking instability, scan-line texture, rain-like dropout, chromatic drift, and occasional exposure wobble. The damage should vary over time rather than becoming a fixed LoRA fingerprint.\n",
    "\n",
    "For footage, colorize representative keyframes first, then propagate or stabilize the color through the shot before adding the VHS treatment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Lore reference\n",
    "\n",
    "Canonical Slayverse index:\n",
    "\n",
    "`C:\\runb2\\VUORSE-VORTEX\\Slayverse\\json\\slayverse_index_minified.json`\n",
    "\n",
    "Relevant Sassy prompt anchors: `sassy mcgraw`, `sassafras aloysius mcgraw`, `first lady of kdfw`, `1970s television news anchor`, `Farrah Fawcett hair`, `brown suede vest`, `white mock turtleneck`, `gold chain necklace`, `golden angel wings brooch`."
   ]
  }
 ],
